The error log indicates a problem with the project configuration file `prj.conf`. The line `CONFIG_MAX_THREAD_BYTES=3` is invalid because the value must be a multiple of `sizeof(void *)`. This is likely causing an early build failure with a misleading error message. I will correct this value to 8, which is a safe value for both 32-bit and 64-bit architectures.

Additionally, there is a latent bug in the test source code related to userspace memory domains. The new test file `src/test_rtio_pool.c` incorrectly sets up its own memory domain, which conflicts with the setup in `src/test_rtio_api.c`. This will cause runtime failures for userspace tests. The fix involves centralizing the memory domain setup in `test_rtio_api.c` and having `test_rtio_pool.c` reuse it. This requires making the setup function and domain variable in `test_rtio_api.c` non-static and then referencing them from `test_rtio_pool.c`.

Finally, there is a minor typo in the copyright year in `src/test_rtio_pool.c`, which I will also correct.

